            </note>
            <note corresp="#d257-f2" n="3" xml:id="d257-f2-content">
                <p>James C. Dunn, Adviser on Political Relations.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d257-f3" n="4" xml:id="d257-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="frus1943CairoTehran#pg_513">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, The Conferences at Cairo and
                        Tehran, 1943, pp. 513</ref>, <ref target="frus1943CairoTehran#pg_854"
                        >854</ref>–<ref target="frus1943CairoTehran#pg_855">855</ref>, <ref
                        target="frus1943CairoTehran#pg_862">862</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1943CairoTehran#pg_863">863</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d257-f4" n="5" xml:id="d257-f4-content">
                <p>Marshal Iosif Vissarionovich Stalin, Chairman of the Council of People’s
                    Commissars of the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d257-f5" n="6" xml:id="d257-f5-content">
                <p>British Prime Minister Winston S. Churchill.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
